  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">100 Scholarships for Girls in Niger!</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Less than 50% of girls in Niger attend primary school, only 11% progress to middle school, and less than 5% matriculate to high school. Keeping girls in school during middle and high school has a positive, cascading effect on their lives, families, and communities. The intended outcome of our Girls Advancement Program is that girls are enabled to continue their secondary education. We aim to ensure that 100 girls are in school and supported for success during the 2023-24 academic year.</narrative>
  </description>
